Priya Nair: FYI opened PR that consolidates SDK snippets & migration guide for streaming/pagination/retries. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/512

Sam Ortiz: Nice. Main change for Python: stream yields ChatChunk objects now instead of raw bytes. Example I added in docs/tests/snippets shows .delta / .text fields.

Sam Ortiz: ```python
from redwood import Client
client = Client(retries=4, retry_backoff='exponential')

# streaming - yields high-level chunks
for chunk in client.chat.stream(model='gpt-4o', input='Summarize this'):
    if chunk.type == 'message':
        print(chunk.delta or chunk.text)
```

Leo Park: TS async iterator mirrors Python: ```ts
import { Client } from 'redwood'
const client = new Client({ retries: 4, retryMode: 'exponential' })

for await (const chunk of client.chat.stream({ model: 'gpt-4o', input: 'Summarize this' })) {
  if (chunk.type === 'message') console.log(chunk.delta ?? chunk.text)
}
```

Denise Wu: For listing APIs we switched to cursor semantics. Go example in docs/snippets:

```go
c := redwood.NewClient()
cursor := ""
for {
  resp, err := c.Responses.List(context.Background(), redwood.ListOptions{Cursor: cursor, PageSize: 100})
  if err != nil {
    log.Fatal(err)
  }
  for _, item := range resp.Items {
    fmt.Println(item.Text)
  }
  if resp.NextCursor == "" {
    break
  }
  cursor = resp.NextCursor
}
```

Priya Nair: Note about mixing streaming + pagination: we intentionally avoided showing combined examples; it's complex and confuses readers. Added short caveat in the migration guide.

Alex Park: Added a small test that Lint/snippets CLI picks up. Also updated the snippet bundler so that language-specific tests run under docs CI.

